WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.342 --> 00:00:02.520
(drums beating)

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.920
- Remember, attack together.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:08.170
Every time I give you a three-four,

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.193
breathe on four, and attack on one.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.220
I put so much love and
effort, sweat and blood,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.723
and tears into this band program.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.983
We are the best marching
band in the country.

00:00:29.315 --> 00:00:31.898
(mellow music)

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.230
My name is Abraham Duffie Jr.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.610
And I am the head drum major

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.210
for the Sonic Boom of the South.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:45.273
We bring something that
no other band brings:

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.963
excitement, jaw-dropping,
in-your-face entertainment.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.820
The Jackson State Drum Majors
are the heart of the band.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.510
We are known for our showmanship,

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:00.260
but what a lot of people don't know

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.780
is we teach music to the band.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:06.640
We lead the band, we help with formations,

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.473
and we also help guide the band.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.940
(chanting)

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.810
And the beginning of August we practice

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.990
for about 20 hours a day

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.173
from 5 a.m. to 12 a.m. in the morning.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.643
You really just have
to find time to sleep.

00:01:28.465 --> 00:01:30.715
(chanting)

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.113
- Exercise!

00:01:34.113 --> 00:01:36.710
(upbeat music)

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.420
- Not only is it physical training,

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.600
it's also mental and
emotional training as well

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.340
that's needed in order
to be a part of a program

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.443
of our caliber.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.720
- What goes on is lot of
playing, a lot of playing,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.760
and a lot of playing.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.150
And also marching.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.083
Marching, marching, marching, marching.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.090
Being in physical shape
gives you endurance.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.210
It helps you play better
and perform better

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:05.028
and also gives you muscle memory.

00:02:05.028 --> 00:02:07.695
(drums beating)

00:02:10.376 --> 00:02:13.459
(band music playing)

00:02:18.974 --> 00:02:21.750
This is my fourth and
final year as Drum Major.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.490
My hope for the future of the band

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:28.490
is to just excel, be better
than the bands before them,

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.443
be better musicians.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.230
Just to finally be at
the end is bittersweet,

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:39.530
but I am going to leave
and never look back,

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.793
because I know I made my mark.

00:02:41.793 --> 00:02:44.043
(applause)

